-- Q416: Intangible Assets [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IAS 38, paragraph 54, research phase costs must always be expensed as incurred because the entity cannot demonstrate that an intangible asset exists that will generate probable future economic benefits. Only development costs may be capitalized when all six criteria in IAS 38.57 are satisfied. This contrasts with ASC 730-10-25, which requires expensing both research and most development costs.
Wrong (B): IAS 38 prohibits capitalizing research costs regardless of expected profitability. The capitalization threshold applies only to development phase costs, not research.
Wrong (C): The six development criteria in IAS 38.57 apply exclusively to development expenditures. Research costs are expensed without reference to those criteria.
Wrong (D): IAS 38 does not permit deferral and amortization of research costs. There is no provision for spreading research expenditures over an arbitrary period.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 416;

